# Frontend environment model of the house (`_standards/backend.md` section 6.2,
# `_standards/frontend.md` section 3.3). Same keys, same order, same blocks in
# every project; only the example values are the project's own.
# `sync-to-project.mjs --check` compares the key list and fails on an extra, a
# missing or a misplaced key. A key the catalog does not have is not added here:
# it goes to the upstream first.

#--------------------------------------------------------------------
# API
#--------------------------------------------------------------------
# Base of the API. In dev it is the port that `backend/pnpm dev` starts.
#
# The `VITE_` prefix is what makes Vite embed the value in the browser bundle,
# that is, publish it. No secret goes in this file: API keys, passwords and
# third-party tokens stay in the backend `.env`, which never reaches the client.
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:3333

# The API address seen from INSIDE the SSR server (service name on the Docker
# network). Read at runtime by Nitro, without `VITE_`: it never reaches the
# browser. In production it is set in the hosting panel; when absent, the server
# uses `VITE_API_URL`.
# SERVER_API_URL=http://api:3333

#--------------------------------------------------------------------
# Site
#--------------------------------------------------------------------
# The public origin of the site, the one that goes into `sitemap.xml` and
# `robots.txt`. No trailing slash. In dev it is the port that
# `frontend/pnpm dev` starts.
VITE_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000

#--------------------------------------------------------------------
# Upload
#--------------------------------------------------------------------
# The per-file ceiling, in bytes: the same `UPLOAD_MAX_SIZE` as the backend
# `.env`. Optional: when absent, the client does not refuse by size and the
# server answers 422.
# Curupira: not read here. The report photo has its own fixed ceiling
# (`LIST_LIMITS.REPORT_PHOTO_SIZE` in `@curupira/shared`), and there is no file library.
# VITE_UPLOAD_MAX_SIZE=1073741824

#--------------------------------------------------------------------
# E2E
#--------------------------------------------------------------------
# Only for `pnpm test:e2e` (Playwright), read from `e2e/support/env.ts` and with
# no default: when one is missing, the run stops and says which. The account is
# the backend seeder's; the password never goes into Git.
# E2E_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3010
# E2E_API_URL=http://localhost:3333
# E2E_OWNER_EMAIL=administrator@example.com
# E2E_OWNER_PASSWORD=
# Optional: a folder outside the repo where the responsive spec saves one
# full-page capture per screen and viewport; unset, it saves none.
# E2E_SHOTS_DIR=/tmp/shots

#--------------------------------------------------------------------
# Curupira: keys the catalog does not have yet (`sync --check` lists them as extra)
#--------------------------------------------------------------------
# `mock` serves `src/data/*` with no backend; `api` talks to `VITE_API_URL`. The single
# switch lives in `src/integrations/tanstack-query/source.ts`. The production build is `api`
# (`frontend/.env.production`, checked by the CI).
VITE_DATA_SOURCE=mock

# Origin of the bucket the browser PUTs each report photo to (presigned URL). The production
# CSP (`vite.config.ts`) only lets `connect-src` and `img-src` reach origins listed here; with
# the bucket in path style it is the `STORAGE_ENDPOINT` of the backend, with virtual-host
# style it is `https://<bucket>.<endpoint host>`. No path, no trailing slash.
VITE_STORAGE_URL=http://localhost:9006
